Do not probe for __declspec() on illumos. It is not supported, and the probes
fail with an implicit int error from gcc 14 and later. That is the correct
result, but it is indistinguishable from a broken configure test and fails the
build system check for those. __attribute__ is tried as well.

diff -wpruN --no-dereference '--exclude=*.orig' a~/tool/m4/ruby_decl_attribute.m4 a/tool/m4/ruby_decl_attribute.m4
--- a~/tool/m4/ruby_decl_attribute.m4	1970-01-01 00:00:00
+++ a/tool/m4/ruby_decl_attribute.m4	1970-01-01 00:00:00
@@ -18,7 +18,6 @@ RUBY_WERROR_FLAG([
 for mac in \
     "__attribute__ ((attrib_code)) x" \
     "x __attribute__ ((attrib_code))" \
-    "__declspec(attrib_code) x" \
     x; do
   m4_ifval([$4],mac="$mac"${rbcv_cond+" /* only if $rbcv_cond */"})
   AC_COMPILE_IFELSE([AC_LANG_PROGRAM([
